<title>SOUTH AFRICA: JCI cautions shareholders on trading.</title>
<headline>JCI cautions shareholders on trading.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-07-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>South African mining house JCI Ltd said on Tuesday that shareholders should continue to exercise caution when dealing in its shares.</p>
<p>The firm had on Monday announced that merger talks between it and Lonrho Plc were terminated, but that other discussions were still ongoing.</p>
<p>&quot;The company confirms that negotiations are continuing regarding other possible transactions...shareholders are advsied therefore to continue to exercise caution in their dealings in JCI Ltd shares until a further announcement is made,&quot; the firm said.</p>
<p>The firm's stock was already trading under cautionary statements announced on May 20 and June 13.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
</text>
